 "statement": "Annotated blind from the Beinecke scan only: canvas 1006204 ('72v (part)') shows two circles; I take the RIGHT one (centre near x=4680, y=1780) as f72v2, the panel nearer the binding (the book block lies at the right of this view). f72v2 and f72v3 share one line structure (18 outer, 12 inner label lines), so the counts cannot settle the order; if the panels are the other way round this annotation belongs to f72v3 (my f72v3 annotation used the same reasoning for the left circle). Drawn: an outer ring of 18 nude female figures without tubs (two at about 2-3 o'clock faint, one at about 8 o'clock very faint and uncertain), an inner ring of 12, matching the label lines; eight-pointed stars beside many figures; in the centre a clothed figure in a blue cap and a long robe with blue folds flaring to the right, one arm forward, a star by the head, a small dotted rosette below, and a word in darker ink to its left that has no label line of its own. No label line id is assigned to a figure (ids carry no position; the words were not read); each figure carries ring, angle, clockwise order and its ring's line ids as candidates.",
